CAT = "maceReport"; SEG = "RPT"
Q = [
("An aide gave a resident's 9 a.m. dose to the wrong resident. What does the model curriculum say the aide does first?",
 'Report it to the nurse at once', ['Wait to see if harm occurs', 'Give the right resident two', 'Report it at the end of the shift'],
 'The model curriculum says an MA-C who believes an error occurred follows facility policy to report it to the appropriate superior, then helps complete the documentation.'),
('After reporting a medication error, what else does the model curriculum expect of the aide?',
 'Help complete the report', ['Correct the MAR to hide it', 'Decide the treatment needed', 'Call the family to explain it'],
 'The aide assists in completing any required documentation of the medication error, such as an incident report. The nurse decides what care the resident needs.'),
('A package insert says to give a drug with a full glass of water, and the aide gives it with a sip. Which cause of error does the model curriculum name for this?',
 "Ignoring the maker's directions", ["Ignoring the prescriber's order", "Ignoring the client's concern", 'Ignoring the facility policy'],
 "Failure to follow the manufacturer's specifications or directions for use is one of the causes of medication errors listed in the model curriculum."),
('A resident says, "That\'s not my usual pill," and the aide gives it anyway. Which listed cause of error is this?',
 'Ignoring her concern', ["Ignoring the maker's label", 'Ignoring a stop date', "Ignoring the prescriber's order"],
 "Failure to listen to a client's or family's concerns is a listed cause of medication errors. The aide stops and checks the order and label again."),
('An aide gives a medication once daily when the order says twice daily. Which listed cause of error is this?',
 'Not following the order', ['Not reading the insert', "Ignoring the client's concern", 'Not asking the pharmacist'],
 "Failure to follow the prescriber's orders exactly is the first cause of medication errors in the model curriculum."),
('Under the model curriculum, which sign must the aide report to the supervising nurse right away?',
 'Life-threatening signs', ['Mild expected side effects', "A resident's diet request", 'Routine vital signs in range'],
 'The model curriculum says the MA-C reports signs or symptoms that appear life-threatening, events that appear health-threatening, and medications that produce no result or undesirable effects.'),
('A resident says his pain pill given two hours ago has not helped at all. What should the aide do?',
 'Let the nurse know', ['Give a second pill now', 'Tell him to wait longer', "Tell the nurse at next week's review"],
 'A medication that produces no result as reported by the client is something the MA-C reports to the supervising nurse, who assesses the pain.'),
("A resident's pulse is much slower than her usual before a heart medication that needs a pulse check. What is the right step?",
 'Hold it and tell the nurse', ['Give it as scheduled', 'Give it, then tell the nurse', 'Recheck it tomorrow'],
 "A change from the client's normal condition, including a pulse change, is reported. The nurse decides whether the dose is given."),
("Which change from a resident's normal condition does the model curriculum list among things to report?",
 'Urine output', ['Bedtime routine', 'Room assignment', 'Visitor schedule'],
 'Other changes to report include urinary output, mental status and activity, alongside temperature, pulse, respirations, blood pressure and pain.'),
('A resident who is usually alert and chatty is suddenly confused after a new medication. What does the aide do?',
 'Tell the nurse right away', ['Wait for the next round', 'Tell the nurse at the next pass', 'Ask her family to sit with her'],
 'A change in mental status is a change from normal to report. The model curriculum says to notify the nurse as soon as possible with as much information as available.'),
("What does the model curriculum say the aide should do after reporting a change in a client's condition?",
 'Record the change', ['Hold the next dose', 'Recheck it next shift', 'Tell the family'],
 'The model curriculum says to observe, monitor and report a change, notify the nurse with as much information as available, and record the change.'),
('A resident develops an itchy rash and lip swelling soon after a new antibiotic. Which response fits?',
 'Get help now for an allergy', ['Apply lotion and wait', 'Give the next dose early', 'Report it at the end of shift'],
 'Lip swelling with a rash can be an allergic reaction that may become anaphylaxis, which is life-threatening, so the nurse is called immediately.'),
('Which information is most useful when an aide reports a side effect to the nurse?',
 'What was seen and when', ["The aide's own diagnosis", 'Which drug to stop', 'A guess at the cause'],
 "The model curriculum asks the aide to notify the nurse with as much information as available. Observations and times help the nurse assess; diagnosing is not the aide's role."),
('A resident feels hot and her temperature is well above her usual reading. What should the aide do?',
 'Report the temperature', ['Give any PRN fever drug', 'Report it if high tomorrow', 'Offer fluids and recheck later'],
 "Temperature is the first vital sign the model curriculum lists for reporting a change from normal. Whether a PRN dose is given is the nurse's judgment."),
('An aide finds that a dose was missed on the previous shift. What should happen?',
 'Report the missed dose', ['Give it with the next dose', 'Chart it as given late', 'Report it only if harm follows'],
 'A missed dose is a medication error. Doubling up can harm the resident, so the aide reports it and the nurse decides what to do.'),
('A nearly given wrong dose is caught by the third safety check. What is the value of reporting near misses too?',
 'Finding system causes', ['Finding who to blame', 'Keeping the count right', 'Closing the incident'],
 'Reports of errors and near misses help a facility find and fix what led to them, such as look-alike packaging or a confusing MAR.'),
('Under the model curriculum, which kind of event does the aide report to the supervising nurse?',
 'Health-threatening events', ['Every dose given on time', 'Meal choices', 'Staffing changes'],
 'The model curriculum lists signs that appear life-threatening, events that appear health-threatening and medications with no result or undesirable effects.'),
("A resident's blood pressure reading before a dose is far lower than usual. What should the aide report?",
 'The reading and the time taken', ['Only that she seemed tired', 'Nothing until it happens again', 'The reading next week'],
 'Blood pressure is one of the vital signs the model curriculum lists for reporting when it changes from normal. Exact numbers and times help the nurse.'),
('A new medication leaves a resident unusually drowsy and unsteady on her feet. Why does this matter most?',
 'It raises her fall risk', ['It shows the dose is too low', 'It means the drug is working', 'It will pass by itself'],
 'Drowsiness and unsteadiness are side effects to report because they can lead to falls. The nurse decides if the order needs review.'),
("Before a heart medication that needs a pulse check, a resident's pulse is inside the range the nurse set for giving it. What should the aide do?",
 'Give it and chart the pulse', ['Hold it and tell the nurse', 'Recheck it in an hour first', 'Give half, then tell the nurse'],
 "A pulse within the nurse's set range is not a change from normal, so the dose is given as ordered and the reading charted. Only a pulse outside that range is held and reported."),
]
